{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_NZwEzL1NiypCM9J6w6ZUt2fV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"task-001\",\n  \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\",\n  \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Complete the openspec CLI commands implementation. IMPORTANT: Your branch is behind master. You MUST first update your branch from master to avoid reverting already-merged changes.\\n\\n**Steps to take:**\\n1. First, merge master into your branch: `git fetch origin && git merge origin/master`\\n2. Resolve any merge conflicts\\n3. Then implement the missing openspec commands\\n\\n**What to implement:**\\n1. `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (creates openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/)\\n2. `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n\\n**Files to read:**\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (for startup protocol references)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see existing command patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes:**\\n- Add commands in tools/se3_tools/commands/openspec.py\\n- Register in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns from other commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n- Run `se3 lint` to ensure specs are valid\\n- Run any tests you create\\n\\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT delete or modify files from other tasks (human_calls.py, archive_calls.py, collab.py changes, etc.). These were already merged to master and must be preserved.\\n\",\n  \"spec_refs\": [\n    \"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\",\n    \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"\n  ],\n  \"dependencies\": [],\n  \"health\": {\n    \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n    \"attempts\": 2,\n    \"max_attempts\": 3,\n    \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:53:42.324701\"\n  },\n  \"started_at\": \"now\",\n  \"worker_pid\": 2508184,\n  \"worker_exit_code\": 1,\n  \"completed_at\": \"now\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcf1454d-d84f-4ded-9596-69a7d6bcc4e5","uuid":"7083f7f2-b39a-46c4-bcce-89ef63bf81af","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"task-001\",\n  \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\",\n  \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Complete the openspec CLI commands implementation. IMPORTANT: Your branch is behind master. You MUST first update your branch from master to avoid reverting already-merged changes.\\n\\n**Steps to take:**\\n1. First, merge master into your branch: `git fetch origin && git merge origin/master`\\n2. Resolve any merge conflicts\\n3. Then implement the missing openspec commands\\n\\n**What to implement:**\\n1. `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (creates openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/)\\n2. `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n\\n**Files to read:**\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (for startup protocol references)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see existing command patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes:**\\n- Add commands in tools/se3_tools/commands/openspec.py\\n- Register in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns from other commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n- Run `se3 lint` to ensure specs are valid\\n- Run any tests you create\\n\\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT delete or modify files from other tasks (human_calls.py, archive_calls.py, collab.py changes, etc.). These were already merged to master and must be preserved.\\n\",\n  \"spec_refs\": [\n    \"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\",\n    \"openspec/spec